IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 5B SPECIAL ADMINISTRATION ORDER: ss 44 to 49.  PART 5C ALTERNATIVE DISPUTE RESOLUTION SCHEME: ss 50 to 52.
-- Seat: the specified telecommunication licensee (or its shareholder or creditor) in Part 5B; the subscriber and the declared telecommunication
-- licensee in Part 5C.  The Minister's and the Authority's powers are expressed as the conditions under which they may be used.
-- Neither Part is in the 2000 Revised Edition (Part 5B was inserted in 2011, Part 5C in 2016).

§ `s 44 Interpretation of Part 5B`

-- src:4372 | 44. In this Part —
-- src:4374 | “critical support infrastructure” means any infrastructure that
-- src:4375 | belongs to, or is under the control of, a telecommunication
-- src:4376 | licensee, and that satisfies all of the following criteria:
-- src:4378 | (a) the infrastructure is required by other
-- src:4379 | telecommunication licensees to provide a
-- src:4380 | telecommunication service;
-- src:4382 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:4383 | 89 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:4385 | (b) the infrastructure cannot be replicated within the
-- src:4386 | foreseeable future, or obtained from a third party, by
-- src:4387 | an efficient new entrant to the market for
-- src:4388 | telecommunication services in Singapore, in either
-- src:4389 | case, at a cost that would reasonably allow market
-- src:4390 | entry;
-- src:4392 | (c) the failure or refusal by the firstmentioned
-- src:4393 | telecommunication licensee to allow other
-- src:4394 | telecommunication licensees to use the
-- src:4395 | infrastructure would unreasonably restrict
-- src:4396 | competition in any market for telecommunication
-- src:4397 | services in Singapore;
@ref s 44 "critical support infrastructure" (src:4372-4397)
GIVEN `it belongs to, or is under the control of, a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is required by other telecommunication licensees to provide a telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it cannot be replicated within the foreseeable future, or obtained from a third party, by an efficient new entrant to the market for telecommunication services in Singapore at a cost that would reasonably allow market entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure or refusal by the licensee to allow other telecommunication licensees to use it would unreasonably restrict competition in a market for telecommunication services in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44: this is "critical support infrastructure"` MEANS
    `it belongs to, or is under the control of, a telecommunication licensee` AND `it is required by other telecommunication licensees to provide a telecommunication service` AND `it cannot be replicated within the foreseeable future, or obtained from a third party, by an efficient new entrant to the market for telecommunication services in Singapore at a cost that would reasonably allow market entry` AND `the failure or refusal by the licensee to allow other telecommunication licensees to use it would unreasonably restrict competition in a market for telecommunication services in Singapore`

-- src:4399 | “prescribed transferee” means —
-- src:4401 | (a) the Authority; or
-- src:4403 | (b) a person nominated by the Authority;
-- src:4405 | “specified telecommunication licensee” means a
-- src:4406 | telecommunication licensee which the Minister has
-- src:4407 | declared under section 45 to be a specified
-- src:4408 | telecommunication licensee for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 44 "prescribed transferee" and "specified telecommunication licensee" (src:4399-4408)
GIVEN `it is the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person nominated by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44: this is a "prescribed transferee"` MEANS
    `it is the Authority` OR `it is a person nominated by the Authority`

GIVEN `it is a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has declared it under section 45 to be a specified telecommunication licensee for the purposes of Part 5B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44: this is a "specified telecommunication licensee"` MEANS
    `it is a telecommunication licensee` AND `the Minister has declared it under section 45 to be a specified telecommunication licensee for the purposes of Part 5B`

§ `s 45 Declaration of specified telecommunication licensee`

-- src:4416 | 45.—(1) The Minister may, after consulting with the Authority, by
-- src:4417 | notification in the Gazette, declare any telecommunication licensee to
-- src:4418 | be a specified telecommunication licensee for the purposes of this
-- src:4419 | Part, if —
-- src:4421 | (a) the licensee —
-- src:4423 | (i) is a public telecommunication licensee; or
-- src:4425 | (ii) owns or controls any critical support infrastructure;
-- src:4426 | or
-- src:4428 | (b) the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest to do
-- src:4429 | so.
@ref s 45(1) (src:4416-4429)
GIVEN `the Minister consulted the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee is a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee owns or controls critical support infrastructure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(1): the Minister may declare the telecommunication licensee to be a specified telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    `the Minister consulted the Authority` AND `the declaration is by notification in the Gazette` AND (`the licensee is a public telecommunication licensee` OR `the licensee owns or controls critical support infrastructure` OR `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest to do so`)

-- src:4436 | (2) A declaration of a specified telecommunication licensee under
-- src:4437 | subsection (1)(a)(i) remains in force only so long as the licensee
-- src:4438 | remains a public telecommunication licensee.
-- src:4440 | [19/2011]
-- src:4442 | (3) A declaration of a specified telecommunication licensee under
-- src:4443 | subsection (1)(a)(ii) remains in force only so long as the licensee
-- src:4444 | continues to own or control any critical support infrastructure.
@ref s 45(2) and (3) (src:4436-4444)
GIVEN `the declaration was made under subsection (1)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee remains a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration was made under subsection (1)(a)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee continues to own or control critical support infrastructure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(2) and (3): the declaration remains in force` MEANS
    ((NOT `the declaration was made under subsection (1)(a)(i)`) OR `the licensee remains a public telecommunication licensee`) AND ((NOT `the declaration was made under subsection (1)(a)(ii)`) OR `the licensee continues to own or control critical support infrastructure`)

-- src:4448 | (4) The Minister may, after consulting with the Authority, by
-- src:4449 | notification in the Gazette, revoke any declaration under
-- src:4450 | subsection (1).
@ref s 45(4) (src:4448-4450)
GIVEN `the Minister consulted the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the revocation is by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(4): the Minister may revoke the declaration` MEANS
    `the Minister consulted the Authority` AND `the revocation is by notification in the Gazette`

§ `s 46 Meaning and effect of special administration order`

-- src:4458 | 46.—(1) A special administration order is an order of the Minister,
-- src:4459 | made in accordance with section 47 in relation to a specified
-- src:4460 | telecommunication licensee, directing that during the period for
-- src:4461 | which the order is in force, the affairs, business and property of that
-- src:4462 | licensee must be managed by a person appointed by the Minister
-- src:4463 | (which may include the Authority) —
-- src:4465 | (a) for securing one or more of the purposes of such an order
-- src:4466 | set out in subsection (2); and
-- src:4468 | (b) in a manner which protects the respective interests of the
-- src:4469 | shareholders and the creditors of the licensee.
@ref s 46(1) (src:4458-4469)
GIVEN `the order is made by the Minister in accordance with section 47 in relation to a specified telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order directs that, during the period for which it is in force, the affairs, business and property of the licensee must be managed by a person appointed by the Minister, which may include the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the management is for securing one or more of the purposes in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the management is in a manner which protects the respective interests of the shareholders and the creditors of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46(1): this is a "special administration order"` MEANS
    `the order is made by the Minister in accordance with section 47 in relation to a specified telecommunication licensee` AND `the order directs that, during the period for which it is in force, the affairs, business and property of the licensee must be managed by a person appointed by the Minister, which may include the Authority` AND `the management is for securing one or more of the purposes in subsection (2)` AND `the management is in a manner which protects the respective interests of the shareholders and the creditors of the licensee`

-- src:4473 | (2) The purposes mentioned in subsection (1)(a) are —
-- src:4475 | (a) the security and reliability of the supply of
-- src:4476 | telecommunication services in Singapore;
-- src:4478 | (b) the survival of the specified telecommunication licensee,
-- src:4479 | or the whole or any part of its business or undertaking, as a
-- src:4480 | going concern;
-- src:4482 | (c) the transfer to another person, or (as respects different parts
-- src:4483 | of its business or undertaking) to 2 or more different
-- src:4484 | persons, as a going concern, of so much of the specified
-- src:4485 | telecommunication licensee’s business or undertaking as it
-- src:4487 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:4488 | 91 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:4490 | is necessary to transfer in order to ensure that the functions
-- src:4491 | and duties which have been vested in the licensee by virtue
-- src:4492 | of its licence may be properly carried out; and
-- src:4494 | (d) the carrying out of the functions and duties vested in the
-- src:4495 | specified telecommunication licensee, pending the making
-- src:4496 | of the transfer and the vesting of those functions and duties
-- src:4497 | in any other person or persons.
@ref s 46(2) (src:4473-4497)
GIVEN purpose IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46(2): this is a purpose of a special administration order` MEANS
    elem purpose (LIST "the security and reliability of the supply of telecommunication services in Singapore"
                       , "the survival of the specified telecommunication licensee, or the whole or any part of its business or undertaking, as a going concern"
                       , "the transfer to another person, or to 2 or more different persons, as a going concern, of so much of the licensee's business or undertaking as is necessary to ensure that the functions and duties vested in the licensee by its licence may be properly carried out"
                       , "the carrying out of the functions and duties vested in the licensee, pending the making of the transfer and the vesting of those functions and duties in any other person or persons")

-- src:4501 | (3) The Minister may make regulations for giving effect to this Part,
-- src:4502 | including —
-- src:4504 | (a) regulations governing the transfer of a specified
-- src:4505 | telecommunication licensee’s business or undertaking
-- src:4506 | mentioned in subsection (2)(c); and
-- src:4508 | (b) where a special administration order is made, regulations
-- src:4509 | for applying, omitting or modifying the provisions of Parts
-- src:4510 | 7 and 9 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution
-- src:4511 | Act 2018.
@ref s 46(3) (src:4501-4511)
GIVEN matter IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46(3): the Minister may make regulations giving effect to Part 5B for this matter` MEANS
    elem matter (LIST "the transfer of a specified telecommunication licensee's business or undertaking mentioned in subsection (2)(c)"
                      , "where a special administration order is made, applying, omitting or modifying the provisions of Parts 7 and 9 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018")

§ `s 47 Power to make special administration order, etc.`

-- src:4520 | 47.—(1) If, on an application made to the Minister by the Authority
-- src:4521 | in relation to any specified telecommunication licensee, the Minister
-- src:4522 | is satisfied that any one or more of the grounds specified in
-- src:4523 | subsection (2) are satisfied in relation to that licensee, the Minister
-- src:4524 | may make any one or more of the following orders:
-- src:4526 | (a) a special administration order in relation to that licensee;
-- src:4528 | (b) an order requiring the licensee immediately to take any
-- src:4529 | action or to do or not to do any act or thing in relation to its
-- src:4530 | business as the Minister may consider necessary;
-- src:4532 | (c) an order appointing a person to advise that licensee in the
-- src:4533 | proper conduct of its business.
@ref s 47(1) (src:4520-4533)
GIVEN `the Authority applied to the Minister in relation to a specified telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that one or more of the grounds in subsection (2) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(1): the Minister may make this order` MEANS
    `the Authority applied to the Minister in relation to a specified telecommunication licensee` AND `the Minister is satisfied that one or more of the grounds in subsection (2) are satisfied`
    AND elem order (LIST "a special administration order in relation to the licensee"
                         , "an order requiring the licensee immediately to take any action or to do or not to do any act or thing in relation to its business as the Minister may consider necessary"
                         , "an order appointing a person to advise the licensee in the proper conduct of its business")

-- src:4540 | (2) The grounds mentioned in subsection (1) are that —
-- src:4542 | (a) there has been, is or is likely to be a contravention by the
-- src:4543 | specified telecommunication licensee of the conditions of
-- src:4544 | its licence or of this Act which is serious enough to make it
-- src:4545 | inappropriate for the licensee to continue to hold the
-- src:4546 | licence;
-- src:4548 | (b) the specified telecommunication licensee is or is likely to
-- src:4549 | be unable to pay its debts;
-- src:4551 | (c) the Minister considers it in the interest of the security and
-- src:4552 | reliability of the supply of telecommunication services in
-- src:4553 | Singapore; and
-- src:4555 | (d) the Minister considers it to be in the public interest.
@ref s 47(2) (src:4540-4555)
GIVEN `there has been, is or is likely to be a contravention by the licensee of the conditions of its licence or of the Act which is serious enough to make it inappropriate for the licensee to continue to hold the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee is or is likely to be unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considers it in the interest of the security and reliability of the supply of telecommunication services in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considers it to be in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(2): a ground in subsection (1) is satisfied` MEANS
    `there has been, is or is likely to be a contravention by the licensee of the conditions of its licence or of the Act which is serious enough to make it inappropriate for the licensee to continue to hold the licence` OR `the licensee is or is likely to be unable to pay its debts` OR `the Minister considers it in the interest of the security and reliability of the supply of telecommunication services in Singapore` OR `the Minister considers it to be in the public interest`

-- src:4559 | (3) The Minister may make a special administration order in
-- src:4560 | relation to a specified telecommunication licensee despite the
-- src:4561 | commencement of —
-- src:4563 | (a) any proceedings relating to the making of an order under
-- src:4564 | section 210 of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71 of the
-- src:4565 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 in
-- src:4566 | relation to the specified telecommunication licensee;
-- src:4568 | (b) any proceedings relating to the making of a judicial
-- src:4569 | management order under the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:4570 | Dissolution Act 2018 in relation to the specified
-- src:4571 | telecommunication licensee;
-- src:4573 | (c) any meeting convened under section 94(7) of the
-- src:4574 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 in
-- src:4575 | relation to the specified telecommunication licensee; or
-- src:4577 | (d) any proceedings under the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:4578 | Dissolution Act 2018 relating to the winding up of the
-- src:4579 | affairs of the specified telecommunication licensee.
@ref s 47(3) (src:4559-4579)
GIVEN `proceedings or a meeting of the kind mentioned in subsection (3)(a) to (d) have commenced in relation to the specified telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(3): the commencement of those proceedings or meeting bars the Minister from making a special administration order` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:4583 | (4) Notice of any application under subsection (1) must be given
-- src:4584 | immediately by the Authority to such persons and in such manner as
-- src:4585 | may be determined by the Authority.
@ref s 47(4) (src:4583-4585)
GIVEN `the Authority gave immediate notice of the application to such persons and in such manner as it determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(4): the Authority has given the notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the Authority gave immediate notice of the application to such persons and in such manner as it determined`

-- src:4592 | (5) Any decision of the Minister under subsection (1) is final.
@ref s 47(5) (src:4592-4592)
GIVEN `the Minister made a decision under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(5): the decision of the Minister is final` MEANS
    `the Minister made a decision under subsection (1)`

-- src:4596 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a specified telecommunication
-- src:4597 | licensee, being a company, is unable to pay its debts if it is deemed to
-- src:4598 | be unable to pay its debts under section 125(2) of the Insolvency,
-- src:4599 | Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 47(6) (src:4596-4599)
GIVEN `the specified telecommunication licensee is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is deemed to be unable to pay its debts under section 125(2) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(6): the licensee is unable to pay its debts for the purposes of section 47` MEANS
    `the specified telecommunication licensee is a company` AND `it is deemed to be unable to pay its debts under section 125(2) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`

-- src:4603 | (7) The Minister may at any time (whether or not the appointment
-- src:4604 | of the person has terminated) fix the remuneration and expenses to be
-- src:4605 | paid by a specified telecommunication licensee to any person
-- src:4606 | appointed by the Minister under subsection (1)(c) to advise the
-- src:4607 | licensee in the proper conduct of its business.
@ref s 47(7) (src:4603-4607)
GIVEN `the person was appointed by the Minister under subsection (1)(c) to advise the licensee in the proper conduct of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(7): the Minister may at any time fix the remuneration and expenses to be paid by the licensee to the person` MEANS
    `the person was appointed by the Minister under subsection (1)(c) to advise the licensee in the proper conduct of its business`

-- src:4611 | (8) Where the Minister issues an order to a specified
-- src:4612 | telecommunication licensee under subsection (1) and the licensee
-- src:4613 | fails to comply with that order, the licensee shall be guilty of an
-- src:4614 | offence.
@ref s 47(8) (src:4611-4614)
GIVEN `the Minister issued an order to the specified telecommunication licensee under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee fails to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(8): the licensee is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the Minister issued an order to the specified telecommunication licensee under subsection (1)` AND `the licensee fails to comply with the order`

§ `ss 48 and 49`

-- src:4622 | 48.—(1) Without limiting sections 46 and 47, a special
-- src:4623 | administration order may provide for the following matters:
-- src:4625 | (a) the transfer of the property, rights and liabilities of a
-- src:4626 | specified telecommunication licensee to one or more
-- src:4627 | prescribed transferees;
-- src:4629 | (b) matters that are consequential or related to any such
-- src:4630 | transfer.
@ref s 48(1) (src:4622-4630)
GIVEN matter IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(1): a special administration order may provide for this matter` MEANS
    elem matter (LIST "the transfer of the property, rights and liabilities of a specified telecommunication licensee to one or more prescribed transferees"
                      , "matters that are consequential or related to any such transfer")

-- src:4634 | (2) If the Minister makes a special administration order providing
-- src:4635 | for any matter mentioned in subsection (1), the Minister must, within
-- src:4636 | 6 months after the making of the order, by notification in the Gazette,
-- src:4637 | establish a scheme for determining the amount of any compensation
-- src:4638 | payable to the specified telecommunication licensee for the transfer
-- src:4639 | of its property, rights and liabilities.
@ref s 48(2) (src:4634-4639)
GIVEN `months after the making of the order that the Minister established, by notification in the Gazette, the scheme for determining the amount of compensation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(2): the Minister has established the scheme in time` MEANS
    `months after the making of the order that the Minister established, by notification in the Gazette, the scheme for determining the amount of compensation` AT MOST 6

-- src:4646 | (3) A scheme established under subsection (2) may provide for —
-- src:4648 | (a) the manner in which any compensation or consideration is
-- src:4649 | to be assessed, including methods of calculation, valuation
-- src:4650 | dates and matters to be taken into account or disregarded
-- src:4651 | when making valuations;
-- src:4653 | (b) the assessment to be made by an independent valuer
-- src:4654 | appointed by the Minister; and
-- src:4656 | (c) the remuneration and expenses of the independent valuer.
@ref s 48(3) (src:4646-4656)
GIVEN matter IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(3): the scheme may provide for this matter` MEANS
    elem matter (LIST "the manner in which any compensation or consideration is to be assessed, including methods of calculation, valuation dates and matters to be taken into account or disregarded when making valuations"
                      , "the assessment to be made by an independent valuer appointed by the Minister"
                      , "the remuneration and expenses of the independent valuer")

-- src:4663 | 49.—(1) Despite any other written law —
-- src:4665 | (a) a specified telecommunication licensee must not be wound
-- src:4666 | up voluntarily without the consent of the Authority;
-- src:4668 | (b) a person must not make any application under section 210
-- src:4669 | of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71 of the Insolvency,
-- src:4670 | Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 in relation to a
-- src:4671 | specified telecommunication licensee, unless that person
-- src:4672 | has served 14 days’ notice in writing of the person’s
-- src:4673 | intention to make that application on the Authority;
-- src:4675 | (c) a person must not make any application for a judicial
-- src:4676 | management order under the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:4677 | Dissolution Act 2018 in relation to a specified
-- src:4678 | telecommunication licensee, unless that person has
-- src:4679 | served 14 days’ notice in writing of the person’s
-- src:4680 | intention to make that application on the Authority;
-- src:4682 | (d) a specified telecommunication licensee must not appoint
-- src:4683 | an interim judicial manager under section 94(3) of the
-- src:4684 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018,
-- src:4685 | unless that licensee has served 14 days’ notice in writing
-- src:4686 | of that licensee’s intention to make the appointment on the
-- src:4687 | Authority;
-- src:4689 | (e) a person must not take any step to enforce any security over
-- src:4690 | a specified telecommunication licensee’s property, unless
-- src:4692 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:4693 | 95 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:4695 | that person has served 14 days’ notice in writing of the
-- src:4696 | person’s intention to take that step on the Authority; and
-- src:4698 | (f) a person must not take any step to enforce any judgment or
-- src:4699 | order of court obtained against a specified
-- src:4700 | telecommunication licensee, unless that person has
-- src:4701 | served 14 days’ notice in writing of the person’s
-- src:4702 | intention to take that step on the Authority.
@ref s 49(1) (src:4663-4702)
GIVEN `the Authority consented to the voluntary winding up of the specified telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person served 14 days' notice in writing on the Authority of the person's intention to make the application, appoint the interim judicial manager, or take the step to enforce the security or the judgment or order of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is a voluntary winding up of the specified telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49(1): the person may do the act in relation to the specified telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the act is a voluntary winding up of the specified telecommunication licensee` THEN `the Authority consented to the voluntary winding up of the specified telecommunication licensee`
           OTHERWISE `the person served 14 days' notice in writing on the Authority of the person's intention to make the application, appoint the interim judicial manager, or take the step to enforce the security or the judgment or order of court`

-- src:4708 | (2) The Authority is a party to —
-- src:4710 | (a) any proceedings relating to the making of an order under
-- src:4711 | section 210 of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71 of the
-- src:4712 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 in
-- src:4713 | relation to a specified telecommunication licensee;
-- src:4715 | (b) any proceedings relating to the making of a judicial
-- src:4716 | management order under the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:4717 | Dissolution Act 2018 in relation to a specified
-- src:4718 | telecommunication licensee;
-- src:4720 | (c) any meeting convened under section 94(7) of the
-- src:4721 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 in
-- src:4722 | relation to a specified telecommunication licensee; and
-- src:4724 | (d) any proceedings under the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:4725 | Dissolution Act 2018 relating to the winding up of the
-- src:4726 | affairs of a specified telecommunication licensee.
@ref s 49(2) (src:4708-4726)
GIVEN `the proceedings or meeting are of a kind mentioned in subsection (2)(a) to (d) in relation to a specified telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49(2): the Authority is a party to the proceedings or meeting` MEANS
    `the proceedings or meeting are of a kind mentioned in subsection (2)(a) to (d) in relation to a specified telecommunication licensee`

-- src:4730 | (3) A court must, when deciding any proceedings mentioned in
-- src:4731 | subsection (2), take into consideration any representations made by
-- src:4732 | the Authority in those proceedings.
@ref s 49(3) (src:4730-4732)
GIVEN `the court is deciding proceedings mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49(3): the court must take into consideration any representations made by the Authority in the proceedings` MEANS
    `the court is deciding proceedings mentioned in subsection (2)`

§ `Part 5C: ss 50 to 52`

-- src:4747 | 50. In this Part, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:4749 | “declared telecommunication licensee” means a
-- src:4750 | telecommunication licensee —
-- src:4752 | (a) that is declared by the Authority to be a
-- src:4753 | telecommunication licensee subject to this Part; or
-- src:4755 | (b) that is within a class of telecommunication licensees
-- src:4756 | declared by the Authority to be a class of
-- src:4757 | telecommunication licensees subject to this Part,
-- src:4759 | and the declaration must be notified in the Gazette;
@ref s 50 "declared telecommunication licensee" (src:4747-4759)
GIVEN `it is a telecommunication licensee declared by the Authority to be a telecommunication licensee subject to Part 5C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is within a class of telecommunication licensees declared by the Authority to be a class subject to Part 5C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50: this is a "declared telecommunication licensee"` MEANS
    (`it is a telecommunication licensee declared by the Authority to be a telecommunication licensee subject to Part 5C` OR `it is within a class of telecommunication licensees declared by the Authority to be a class subject to Part 5C`) AND `the declaration is notified in the Gazette`

-- src:4761 | “dispute resolution scheme” means a dispute resolution scheme
-- src:4762 | established or approved by the Authority under section 51(1);
-- src:4764 | “subscriber” means an end user that subscribes to a
-- src:4765 | telecommunication service from a telecommunication
-- src:4766 | licensee.
@ref s 50 "dispute resolution scheme" and "subscriber" (src:4761-4766)
GIVEN `it is a dispute resolution scheme established or approved by the Authority under section 51(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50: this is a "dispute resolution scheme"` MEANS
    `it is a dispute resolution scheme established or approved by the Authority under section 51(1)`

GIVEN `the person is an end user that subscribes to a telecommunication service from a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50: the person is a "subscriber"` MEANS
    `the person is an end user that subscribes to a telecommunication service from a telecommunication licensee`

-- src:4774 | 51.—(1) The Authority may establish or approve one or more
-- src:4775 | dispute resolution schemes for the resolution of disputes between
-- src:4776 | subscribers and declared telecommunication licensees, arising from
-- src:4777 | or relating to the provision of telecommunication services by the
-- src:4778 | declared telecommunication licensees to the subscribers.
@ref s 51(1) (src:4774-4778)
GIVEN `the scheme is for the resolution of disputes between subscribers and declared telecommunication licensees, arising from or relating to the provision of telecommunication services by the licensees to the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(1): the Authority may establish or approve the dispute resolution scheme` MEANS
    `the scheme is for the resolution of disputes between subscribers and declared telecommunication licensees, arising from or relating to the provision of telecommunication services by the licensees to the subscribers`

-- src:4782 | (2) Every declared telecommunication licensee must participate in
-- src:4783 | a dispute resolution scheme and must comply with such terms and
-- src:4784 | conditions of participation in the scheme as may be prescribed.
@ref s 51(2) (src:4782-4784)
GIVEN `the licensee is a declared telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee participates in a dispute resolution scheme and complies with the prescribed terms and conditions of participation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(2): the declared telecommunication licensee has done what the subsection requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee is a declared telecommunication licensee`) OR `the licensee participates in a dispute resolution scheme and complies with the prescribed terms and conditions of participation`

-- src:4791 | (3) To avoid doubt, this Part does not affect the operation of the
-- src:4792 | Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003.
@ref s 51(3) (src:4791-4792)
GIVEN `the Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003 would otherwise operate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(3): Part 5C affects the operation of the Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:4800 | 52. The Authority may, with the approval of the Minister, make
-- src:4801 | regulations under section 97 to provide for matters relating to the
-- src:4802 | operations of an operator of a dispute resolution scheme, including —
-- src:4804 | (a) the standards or requirements of the services provided
-- src:4805 | under the dispute resolution scheme;
-- src:4807 | (b) the fees that the operator may charge for the services
-- src:4808 | provided under the dispute resolution scheme;
-- src:4810 | (c) the records that the operator must keep and the period of
-- src:4811 | retention of such records;
-- src:4813 | (d) the reports that the operator must submit to the Authority,
-- src:4814 | and the manner and time for such submission;
-- src:4816 | (e) matters relating to the administration of the dispute
-- src:4817 | resolution scheme; and
-- src:4819 | (f) generally to give effect to or for carrying out the purposes
-- src:4820 | of this Part.
@ref s 52 (src:4800-4820)
GIVEN `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52: the Authority may make regulations under section 97 for this matter relating to the operations of an operator of a dispute resolution scheme` MEANS
    `the Minister approved`
    AND elem matter (LIST "the standards or requirements of the services provided under the dispute resolution scheme"
                         , "the fees that the operator may charge for the services provided under the dispute resolution scheme"
                         , "the records that the operator must keep and the period of retention of such records"
                         , "the reports that the operator must submit to the Authority, and the manner and time for such submission"
                         , "matters relating to the administration of the dispute resolution scheme"
                         , "generally to give effect to or for carrying out the purposes of Part 5C")
